{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Hadar</b> — The generations declare Your mighty deeds that are seen, and I will meditate upon them with my heart." "<b>The glory of the splendor of Your majesty</b> — The essence of the glory of Your mighty deeds that are seen, as well as the accounts of Your wonders that the generations do not understand."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 145, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:46.534781538Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}